{"title":"Secure Development Tournament","startsAt":"2026-10-05T18:30:00-04:00","endsAt":"2026-10-05T20:30:00-04:00","status":"ACTIVE","type":"PHYSICAL","description":"**What Is a SecureFlag Tournament?**\nAttendees will compete to solve hands-on coding labs in a time-bound challenge inside fully provisioned hands-on development environments. The goal of the competition is to identify vulnerabilities in running applications, then write and submit fixes that must pass both security and functional tests. A live leaderboard will track progress in real time, and the top three performers win gift cards from SecureFlag.\n\n**Why It Works**\n● Capture the Flag format, Reimagined: Instead of only hacking, secure the flag! Fix real vulnerabilities in real code, and learn by doing!\n● No setup required: Just bring a laptop and scan a QR code. Labs run in the browser with everything pre-configured. No local installs. No VMs. No wasted time.\n● Relevant to every developer. With 50+ supported technologies including Python, Java, AWS, Kubernetes, and Terraform, there is a wide selection of challenges available.\n● All skill levels are welcome. Labs range from beginner to advanced. A built-in hint system helps those who get stuck, while experienced developers can push for maximum points with minimal hints and no retries.\n● Competitive leaderboards, prizes, and pizza!\n\n**FAQ**\n\n* What do I need to bring?\n* A laptop and power cord.\n* Will my email be shared with the organizers?\n* Yes! To sign-up for the lab you will need to share your email address. Collected emails will not be used for marketing purposes.\n* Is this in-person only?\n* Yes, to provide the best possible experience.","venue":{"name":"Security Compass","address":"325 Front Street West, Unit 103, Toronto, ON M5V 2Y1, Toronto","lat":43.643295,"lng":-79.3901,"city":"Toronto"},"fee":null,"group":"OWASP Toronto Chapter","image":"https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/9/4/2/8/highres_536317928.jpeg"}